OTPRunner: your two-factor codes, one keystroke away
====================================================

TOTP codes in KRunner, with the secrets kept in your system keystore (KWallet or the
Secret Service). Type "otp git", press Enter, and the code is in your clipboard.

- Add accounts straight from KRunner: select the QR code on screen, paste it, or show it
  to the webcam.
- Import and export otpauth:// links and Google Authenticator transfer codes, including QR
  codes to move your accounts to your phone.
- A full command line tool too.

HOW TO INSTALL
--------------

Do not use the Install button: this entry does not install anything. If you press it, a
terminal opens with these same instructions and nothing else is done.

OTPRunner is installed from PyPI with pipx:

    sudo apt install pipx        # Debian/Ubuntu; use your distribution's package otherwise
    pipx install OTPRunner
    otprunner install            # registers the KRunner plugin and the user service

Then open KRunner and type "otp add".

To remove it: "otprunner uninstall", then "pipx uninstall otprunner". Your secrets stay in
the keystore.

Tested daily on Plasma 5.27 with X11.

Source, screenshots and documentation: https://github.com/baquilla/otprunner
